<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Kasadi Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1881 CE (approx.) · capital Mukalla</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A dynasty of Yafa'i origin that ruled the Hadrami port of Mukalla until the Qu'aiti sultans took it in 1881.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Kasadi were a family of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yafa">Yafa</a> tribal confederation, whose men served as soldiers across <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hadramawt">Hadramawt</a>. In the 18th century they established themselves as naqibs, or governors, of the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukalla">Mukalla</a> on the coast of Hadramawt and ruled it as a small independent state.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukalla">Mukalla</a> was the main outlet of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hadramawt">Hadramawt</a> to the sea, and the Kasadi lived from customs on trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a>, including slaves and dates. Their rule was contested by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kathiri-sultanate">Kathiri</a> and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yafa">Yafa</a>'i rivals and depended on armed retainers. Little is recorded about their internal administration.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 19th century the Kasadi came into conflict with the rising <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/quaiti-sultanate">Qu'aiti Sultanate</a>. With British support the Qu'aiti took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukalla">Mukalla</a> in 1881, and the Kasadi naqib went into exile in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar">Zanzibar</a>. Mukalla became the Qu'aiti capital.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1700 CE – 1881 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34